  "summary": "Install-time fetch-and-execute of remote shell script via dependency-manager script",
  "details": "The package ships scripts/dependency-manager.js which invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...') to fetch and execute a shell installer from a mutable GitHub raw URL. The script also reads os.homedir() and process.platform, uses https.get to reach https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, and uses fs to read/write files. The fetched install.sh is retrieved from a mutable master branch with no pinning or integrity check, so its contents can change at any time and would run under the installing user's account. The bin/awk.js entrypoint additionally combines child_process, curl invocations, and multiple POST/fetch calls, extending the install/run-time execution surface.",
